 "notes": "95%-credible upper limits on kinetic mixing epsilon vs dark-photon mass from Fig. 4 (dark blue 'This signal' curve), from the SuperMAG geomagnetic-data search summarized in Sec. IV (details in companion paper). Curve recovered from the vector figure limit_theory.pdf in the arXiv e-print; axes calibrated to tick labels (x: 3e-18, 1e-17, 6e-17 eV; y: 1e-6..1e-2). The raw limit is a dense, highly jagged band (~10^4 vertices, one limit per searched frequency over 6e-4 to 2e-2 Hz); reported points are medians of the raw curve in 100 log-spaced mass bins, which agree with the paper's own sliding-average ('This signal, smoothed') curve to within ~12%. Individual raw limit values fluctuate around this trend (about 78% lie within a factor of 2). Assumes dark photon is all of DM with rho = 0.3 GeV/cm^3 and SHM velocity dispersion.",
